{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Then Jacob was afraid, and it says, etc.</b> Meaning: he entered the frame of either killing or being killed. Therefore, corresponding to being killed — <b>he was greatly afraid</b>; and corresponding to killing — <b>and it distressed him</b>. And therefore the verse does not say מְאֹד after ״וַיֵּצֶר״." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that since they informed him that Esau dissembles to show brotherhood while he is a hater, Jacob was afraid to prepare himself for war — lest Esau kill him and Jacob has no weapons in his hand — and to prepare himself with weapons <b>distressed him</b>, for it is possible that Esau intends no evil, and when he sees him prepared with weapons Esau will say: is it not Jacob who seeks evil? And through this he will renew his hatred. And therefore he acted wisely — <b>and he divided</b>, etc. Meaning, he divided the people: the first half showed a face of love and affection like a brother to his brother, and half the camp was prepared and armed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:33.053151498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}